// agentshim.core.v1 — the vendor-neutral core of the agent-shim protocol.
//
// SEMANTICS (normative):
//
// - Every UDS hop in the system carries length-prefixed binary messages from
//   this schema set (frontends receive the frontend.v1 package as protojson).
// - The store round-trip: producers (agent-shim stream plane, shim-claude-sidecar
//   file plane) write PERSISTENT Events to the shim-store via StoreWrite; the
//   store assigns Event.seq per session in arrival order, dedups on
//   Event.dedup_key, persists, and fans out to subscribers. The daemon only
//   ever consumes the store-merged stream forwarded by the shim — everything
//   the daemon sees (except EPHEMERAL class) is already durable.
// - EPHEMERAL class (ContentDelta, HeartbeatProgress) bypasses the store:
//   shim → daemon directly. Consumers reconcile per Claude message id,
//   REPLACING a streamed preview with the store-delivered final message.
//   MessageLatency is PERSISTENT because timing analysis needs it on replay.
//   Ephemeral events are never persisted and never replayed.
// - Replay handshake: the shim sends the store Subscribe{session_id,
//   from_seq}; the store replays persisted events with seq > from_seq, then
//   live-tails. The daemon does NOT send this: its resume position rides
//   DaemonHello.from_seq, inside the one bring-up gate (see ShimHello).
// - Bounded historical replay: ReplayRequest{from_seq, to_seq} asks for a
//   one-shot RANGE without moving the standing subscription. Its events come
//   back wrapped in ReplayEvent, a distinct message type so replayed history
//   can never be mistaken for live state, and the range is closed by exactly
//   one ReplayDone.
// - Correlation: any control message carries request_id; asynchronous
//   consequences echo it in Event.request_id where attributable. Ack/Nack is
//   the synchronous receipt on the connection the request arrived on.
// - Turn lifecycle authority: only the live shim's STREAM plane emits
//   TurnStarted / TurnEnded. File-plane stop-hook records remain vendor
//   evidence and never move lifecycle state. Each newly produced turn boundary
//   carries the same non-empty turn_id, equal to the accepted SubmitPrompt's
//   request_id, so an end can close only the turn it names. Historical
//   persisted boundaries produced before turn_id existed have it empty and
//   retain their original ordered-replay semantics. A vendor-session rotation
//   may emit TurnClaimBridge as persistent correlation evidence; it is not a
//   lifecycle boundary and its only consumer is the durable turn ledger.
// - Sad path: a producer that cannot reach the store hard-fails the write,
//   loud-logs every dropped event, and reports DegradedState. No spill
//   buffers, no fallbacks (metaprompt no-fallbacks rule).
//
